    "description": "Nokomis Energy develops and owns distributed solar projects connected to local distribution grids in the United States. Its end markets include community solar programs, local power purchasers, and other distributed-energy counterparties, and the business follows an asset-heavy development-to-own model. Public materials tied to Great Bay Renewables' 2024 investment describe a 77-project solar portfolio across seven U.S. states, with activity focused on distributed generation markets. The disclosed transaction was structured as growth capital to support construction and expansion rather than as a publicly detailed sale of control. Great Bay Renewables announced a $30 million investment in August 2024, and Great Bay is jointly controlled by Altius Renewable Royalties and Apollo-affiliated funds, while public sources do not disclose Nokomis's broader ownership split.",
